1
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:05,757
In Curio's lab, Noah brings a magnet closer…

2
00:00:05,807 --> 00:00:06,132
click!

3
00:00:06,182 --> 00:00:07,948
The paper clips jump onto it.

4
00:00:07,998 --> 00:00:10,691
How does it do that, without touching them?

5
00:00:11,515 --> 00:00:14,321
Mila tries everything: a key, hop!

6
00:00:14,371 --> 00:00:15,328
A nail, hop!

7
00:00:15,378 --> 00:00:17,848
But the copper coin, the cork,

8
00:00:17,898 --> 00:00:20,502
the plastic toy: nothing moves.

9
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:22,806
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:25,335 --> 00:00:25,894
Mini mode!

11
00:00:25,944 --> 00:00:28,631
Around the magnet there is an invisible zone:

12
00:00:28,681 --> 00:00:29,787
the magnetic field.

13
00:00:29,837 --> 00:00:32,403
It is strongest at the two ends, the poles,

14
00:00:32,453 --> 00:00:34,522
and it goes through air and paper.

15
00:00:35,359 --> 00:00:37,801
Iron is full of tiny magnets in a jumble.

16
00:00:37,851 --> 00:00:39,563
The magnet comes closer: hop,

17
00:00:39,613 --> 00:00:41,386
they all line up the same way!

18
00:00:41,436 --> 00:00:42,967
The iron becomes a magnet,

19
00:00:43,017 --> 00:00:44,232
and it is pulled in.

20
00:00:45,021 --> 00:00:46,760
In copper, gold or plastic,

21
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:49,343
there are no tiny magnets that line up.

22
00:00:49,393 --> 00:00:52,109
So the magnet has no grip: nothing moves.

23
00:00:52,922 --> 00:00:53,812
And two magnets?

24
00:00:53,862 --> 00:00:55,459
Same pole against same pole,

25
00:00:55,509 --> 00:00:56,988
they push each other away.

26
00:00:57,038 --> 00:00:57,929
Turn one around…

27
00:00:57,979 --> 00:00:59,625
clack, they grab each other!

28
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,824
That's how a magnet attracts metal.

29
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:06,514
The magnet lines up the tiny magnets inside iron:

30
00:01:06,564 --> 00:01:09,277
the iron becomes a magnet too, and it is pulled in.

31
00:01:10,085 --> 00:01:12,1000
With an adult: paper clips on a sheet of paper,

32
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:14,261
a magnet underneath.

33
00:01:14,311 --> 00:01:16,091
They slide all by themselves!

34
00:01:16,141 --> 00:01:18,159
Try with a copper coin: nothing.

35
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:21,103
And what is hidden inside the Earth?

36
00:01:21,153 --> 00:01:22,383
The answer tomorrow.
